{
	"_": "THE SHARED QUIET-GROUP PARITY FIXTURE (quiet-turn design §5, rev 2). This file is the ONE definition's cross-client contract: the UI's `quietGroupsOf`/`quietGroupOfSegment` (turn-collapse-model.ts) are checked against it by scripts/turn-collapse-model.test.mjs today, and the native, relay-web and TUI group slices COPY this file and check their own derivation against the same cases, the way local-operator's `format.parity.json` and `spend-context.parity.json` pin a formatter across surfaces. A group is client-derived: there is no wire kind and no capability flag, so this fixture - not a schema - is what keeps the clients from drifting apart in silence.",
	"vocabulary": "Rows are records in the UI's `TranscriptRecord` vocabulary, carrying only the fields the group definition reads: `kind` plus (`ts`, `id`) and, per kind, `text` (user/wake/assistant/notice/custom), `body`+`sender` (peer; missing sender fields fall back to the identity ladder), `customType`+`level` (custom), `toolName`+`phase`+`isError` (tool), `complete` (notice). A client with a different record type maps these onto its own shape; the DERIVATION is the shared thing.",
	"shape": "Each case's `expected` is what the group entry point returns: for cases with a `span` (`[from, to]` indexes into `rows`, plus optional `spanHeadLoaded`/`open`), `quietGroupOfSegment(records, span, options)`; otherwise the whole-array `quietGroupsOf(records)`. Timestamps are ms epoch, copied verbatim into `firstTs`/`lastTs`.",
	"generatedBy": "authored by hand for local-operator-ui S2 (quiet-turn slice), 2026-10-10; every case is also exercised through the shipped plan in scripts/turn-collapse-model.test.mjs.",
